  "interpretation": [
    "The analysis measures tracked traffic activity within the tested video windows.",
    "Vehicle observations are not equivalent to unique physical vehicles.",
    "Unique vehicle tracks provide a stronger measure than raw detections.",
    "Persistent tracks provide temporal evidence that vehicles remain observable across frames.",
    "GPS provides route localization and camera/platform movement context where available.",
    "GPS-unavailable windows are explicitly retained rather than assigned fabricated coordinates.",
    "Traffic intelligence score is a prototype ranking and is not a validated congestion ground truth.",
    "Final congestion claims require validation against real traffic conditions or labeled traffic data."
  ],
  "presentation_message": "Marg Dharshak combines vehicle detection, multi-object tracking, temporal persistence and GPS route context to identify traffic-intensity hotspots from moving public-transport camera footage."
}